  "notes": "West leads the ♥2 against 6♥. It looks like the heart lead should be won in dummy and either a spade or a club finesse should be taken. If South takes a losing finesse, his chances of success will be the same regardless of which finesse he takes.\n\nThe same is not true if a winning finesse is taken. If the club finesse wins, South will be in better shape than if the spade finesse is a success because he will have better elimination chances.\n\nAfter the ♣Q wins, South draws a second round of trump and cashes the ♣A. South crosses in trumps and plays North's last club, ruffing in hand. South now crosses to the ♦A and plays a low diamond. If East has a doubleton ♦K, South will have a good diamond on which to discard one of North's spades.\n\nIf East follows with a low diamond, South plays the ♦J. If West started with a doubleton ♦K he will be endplayed. If South's ♦J holds, he exits a diamond and hopes that diamonds are 3-3. If either defender has 4 diamonds including the ♦K, South will need East to have the ♠K.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
    "West leads the ♥2 against 6♥. It looks like the heart lead should be won in dummy and either a spade or a club finesse should be taken. If South takes a losing finesse, his chances of success will be the same regardless of which finesse he takes.",
    "The same is not true if a winning finesse is taken. If the club finesse wins, South will be in better shape than if the spade finesse is a success because he will have better elimination chances.",
    "After the ♣Q wins, South draws a second round of trump and cashes the ♣A. South crosses in trumps and plays North's last club, ruffing in hand. South now crosses to the ♦A and plays a low diamond. If East has a doubleton ♦K, South will have a good diamond on which to discard one of North's spades.",
    "If East follows with a low diamond, South plays the ♦J. If West started with a doubleton ♦K he will be endplayed. If South's ♦J holds, he exits a diamond and hopes that diamonds are 3-3. If either defender has 4 diamonds including the ♦K, South will need East to have the ♠K."
  ],
